  "rationale": "Four blocks suffice, for example jumpHost:lateralMovement, backupHost:lateralMovement, monitoringHost:lateralMovement and fileServer:lateralMovement. Blocking jumpHost and backupHost kills codeRepo. Blocking monitoringHost and fileServer kills mailArchive. domainAdmin needs fileServer, so it dies, and with monitoringHost blocked dbReplica dies too. For shareMount, jumpHost is blocked, serviceAccount needs monitoringHost and localAdmin needs jumpHost, so all three parents are dead. Three blocks are not enough. mailArchive has the entry-fed OR parent fileServer, so one block must go to mailArchive or fileServer. codeRepo can be reached through backupHost, whose parent kerberoast is fed directly by entries, so one block must go to codeRepo, backupHost or kerberoast. The single block left would have to cut both dbReplica and shareMount. dbReplica needs dbReplica or monitoringHost blocked, or both vpnSession and ssoLogin. shareMount needs shareMount or jumpHost blocked, or sshKey, configSecret and vpnSession together. No single step does both, so the minimum is 4."
